    "cause": "Native HTTP initialized its expected byte count from the media response and discarded the exact size already validated by source preflight. A missing or shorter Content-Length could therefore redefine a 24-second recording as a valid 3.94-second file.",
    "fix": "Carry the verified source byte length into NativeHttpClient. Reject initial 200/206 representation lengths that differ from that proof. Use the verified count to check EOF and resume ranges when the media response omits Content-Length. Preserve existing behavior for streams without a verified length.",
    "catalogueDurationUsedAsFailureHeuristic": false,
    "newHTTPUnitRegressions": [
      "verified_initial_length_checks_close_delimited_eof_and_accepts_complete_body",
      "verified_initial_length_rejects_changed_200_and_206_representations",
      "unverified_unknown_length_streams_keep_close_delimited_behavior"
    ]
  },
